-- Notifications (#194, #23 part 1). `notification` and `notification_pref` are tenant tables built
-- with tenantTable(): NOT NULL workspace_id referencing organization ON DELETE cascade, a
-- workspace_id-led index, and ENABLE + FORCE RLS with `ws_isolation` at the end of this migration
-- (exactly what tenantPolicy() emits). Rows are also owned by one user; the notifications service
-- filters by user inside the workspace. notification_dedupe_uq drops repeats of a dedupe_key per
-- member and workspace. `push_subscription` (per user) and `email_suppression` (per address) are
-- global tables (GLOBAL_TABLES) without RLS; the push and email services check ownership.
-- New tables and types only: nothing existing is altered or dropped.
